diff --git a/README.md b/README.md
index d532f62..fa116f1 100644
--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -3,13 +3,25 @@
 A small command-line task tracker that stores tasks in a JSON file.
 
 ```
-tasker add [-p N] <title words...>     add a task (priority 1-5, default 3)
-tasker list [--all] [--sort id|priority] list open tasks (or all)
+tasker add [-p N] [--tag T]... [--due YYYY-MM-DD] <title words...>
+                                                    add a task (priority 1-5, default 3)
+tasker list [--all] [--tag T]... [--overdue] [--sort id|priority|due]
+                                                    list open tasks (or all)
 tasker done <id>                        mark a task done
 tasker rm <id>                          delete a task
-tasker edit <id> [-p N] [--title T]     change priority or title
+tasker edit <id> [-p N] [--title T] [--tag T] [--untag T] [--due YYYY-MM-DD|none]
+                                          change priority, title, tags or due date
+tasker tags                             list every tag used by open tasks with its count
 ```
 
+`--tag` is repeatable. Tags are lower-cased and must match `^[a-z0-9][a-z0-9-]*$`.
+Due dates are stored as UTC midnight. `--overdue` selects open tasks whose due date
+is before today. `--sort due` orders by due date ascending (tasks with no due date
+last, ties by ID). `--due none` in `edit` clears the due date.
+
+List lines show `(due YYYY-MM-DD)` and `[tag1,tag2]` when present, e.g.
+`#4 [ ] P2 file taxes (due 2026-04-15) [home,money]`.
+
 The data file is `$TASKER_FILE` (default `tasks.json` in the current directory).
 
 ## Layout
